fn page_home() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"hero\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"hero-grid\"> <div> <p class=\"eyebrow\">RUDRA 1.1.0</p> <h1>More Than Just a Language. A Platform for the Future.</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nRUDRA is a compiled, statically typed systems language whose compiler is\n            written in RUDRA itself. Write a source file, compile it straight to a\n            native x86-64 Linux executable, and ship. Clean syntax, compile-time\n            type checking, and runtime safety checks.\n</p> <div class=\"hero-actions\"> <a class=\"btn btn-primary btn-lg\" href=\"/downloads/\"> <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M5 21h14\"></path></svg>\nDownload RUDRA\n</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost btn-lg\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/\">Read Documentation</a> </div> <div class=\"hero-meta\"> <span><strong>Linux x86_64</strong> native ELF</span> <span><strong>v1.1.0</strong> latest release</span> <span><strong>Free</strong> to use</span> </div> </div> <div class=\"hero-visual\"> <div class=\"terminal\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Terminal compiling and running a RUDRA program\"> <div class=\"terminal-bar\"> <span class=\"terminal-dot\" style=\"background:#ff5f57\"></span> <span class=\"terminal-dot\" style=\"background:#febc2e\"></span> <span class=\"terminal-dot\" style=\"background:#28c840\"></span> <span class=\"terminal-title\">hello.rux</span> </div> <div class=\"terminal-body\"> <div><span class=\"t-key\">fn</span> <span class=\"t-cmd\">main</span>() -&gt; <span class=\"t-key\">int</span> &#123;</div> <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class=\"t-cmd\">print</span>(<span class=\"t-str\">\"Hello, RUDRA!\\n\"</span>);</div> <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class=\"t-key\">return</span> 0;</div> <div>&#125;</div> <div><span class=\"t-key\">return</span> main();</div> <div class=\"t-dim\">&nbsp;</div> <div><span class=\"t-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"t-cmd\">rudra hello.rux hello &amp;&amp; ./hello</span></div> <div class=\"t-cmd\">Hello, RUDRA!</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"section-tight\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"stat-row\"> <div class=\"stat\"><b>Native</b><span>Direct-to-ELF backend</span></div> <div class=\"stat\"><b>Typed</b><span>Compile-time checking</span></div> <div class=\"stat\"><b>Static</b><span>Zero-dependency ELF</span></div> <div class=\"stat\"><b>Verified</b><span>Evidence-backed claims</span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"section-head\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Capabilities</p> <h2>Built for systems work</h2> <p class=\"lead\">A focused language surface, verified against the shipped toolchain.</p> </div> <div class=\"grid grid-3\"> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M4 7l6 5-6 5M13 17h7\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Native compilation</h3> <p>Compile a <code>.rux</code> file straight to a native Linux x86-64 executable. The compiler is a static ELF written in RUDRA: no C compiler, assembler or linker needed.</p> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M12 3l8 4v5c0 5-3.5 8-8 9-4.5-1-8-4-8-9V7z\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Memory-safety oriented</h3> <p>Statically typed with compile-time checking, bounds-checked list access and a trap on integer division by zero.</p> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"7\" r=\"3\"></circle><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"17\" r=\"3\"></circle><path d=\"M7 10v4a3 3 0 003 3h4\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Channels and processes</h3> <p>Standard-library modules for FIFO channels (<code>chan</code>) and fork-based processes (<code>thread</code>).</p> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"4\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" rx=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M3 9h18\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Structs and enums</h3> <p>Model data with structs and tagged enums, with exhaustiveness-checked pattern matching.</p> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"9\"></circle><path d=\"M3 12h18M12 3a15 15 0 010 18\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Networking and JSON</h3> <p>Socket, HTTP-helper, DNS (IPv4) and JSON modules in the standard library. Authenticated HTTPS is not available yet.</p> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <div class=\"card-icon\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M9 11l3 3 8-8M4 12v6a2 2 0 002 2h12\"></path></svg></div> <h3>Honest status</h3> <p>Every capability is labeled verified, partially verified or planned, with published evidence.</p> </div> </div> <p style=\"text-align:center;margin-top:1.8rem\"><a href=\"/features\">Explore all features</a></p> </div> </section> <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"section-head\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Ecosystem</p> <h2>One language, a modular ecosystem</h2> <p class=\"lead\">Each component is presented independently with an accurate status.</p> </div> <div class=\"grid grid-4\"> <a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/language\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">RUDRA Language</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">A compiled systems language with an easy, readable syntax.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/compiler\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Compiler</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">Source to native binary, directly.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/runtime\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Runtime</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">A minimal native execution model.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/standard-library\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Standard Library</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">Standard-library modules for everyday systems work.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/ruxel-studio\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-off\">NOT VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Ruxel Studio</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">A terminal IDE for RUDRA (source repository).</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/toolchain\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Developer Toolchain</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">Compiler and wrapper released; more tools in the source repository.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/ai-integration\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-planned\">PLANNED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">AI Integration</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">Planned tooling for AI-assisted development.</p> </a><a class=\"card\" href=\"/ecosystem/security\" style=\"display:block\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3 style=\"font-size:1.05rem\">Security Capabilities</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.88rem\">Memory-safety oriented language design.</p> </a> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container narrow\"> <div class=\"section-head\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Get started in minutes</p> <h2>Install and run</h2> </div> <pre class=\"codeblock\"><code>tar -xzf rudra-1.1.0-selfhost-linux-x86_64.tar.gz\ncd rudra-1.1.0-selfhost-linux-x86_64 &amp;&amp; ./install.sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\"\n\nrudra hello.rux hello\n./hello</code></pre> <div class=\"hero-actions\" style=\"justify-content:center;margin-top:1.6rem\"> <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"/downloads/\">Download for Linux</a> <a class=\"btn btn-ghost\" href=\"/docs/installation/\">Installation guide</a> </div> </div> </section> <section class=\"section-tight\"> <div class=\"container\"> <div class=\"grid grid-3\"> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Documentation</h3> <p>Guides, syntax reference and a verified standard-library overview.</p> <a href=\"/docs/getting-started/\">Read the docs</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Transparency</h3> <p>The exact verified feature matrix with evidence and limitations.</p> <a href=\"/transparency\">See verification</a> </div> <div class=\"card\"> <h3>Community</h3> <p>Discussion, help and showcases on GitHub Discussions.</p> <a href=\"/community\">Join in</a> </div> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_login() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\" style=\"max-width:520px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;padding:4rem 0\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Account</p> <h1>No accounts</h1> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin:1rem auto\">\nThis site is static and has no accounts or sign-in. Documentation and\n        compiler downloads are free and need no account.\n</p> <p style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\"><a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra\" rel=\"noopener\">Open the GitHub repository</a></p> <p style=\"margin-top:2rem;font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-dim)\">\nDiscussion and help happen on GitHub Discussions, where GitHub handles\n        authentication under its own policies.\n</p> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_playground() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Try RUDRA</p> <h1>Playground</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nBrowse real RUDRA programs and the output they actually produce. Each\n        sample below was compiled and run with the RUDRA 1.1.0 toolchain.\n</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:1.2rem\"> <h4>How this works</h4> <p>\nRUDRA compiles to native machine code, so there is no in-browser\n          compiler. This page shows verified sample programs and their recorded\n          output. To run your own code, install the toolchain and use\n<code>rudra file.rux program</code> and then run <code>./program</code>. Nothing here is simulated: the\n          output shown is the real output of each sample.\n</p> </div> <div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>hello.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">fn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(&quot;Hello, RUDRA!\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">Hello, RUDRA!</pre></div></div><div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>factorial.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">fn factorial(n: int) -&gt; int {\n    if n &lt;= 1 {\n        return 1;\n    }\n    return n * factorial(n - 1);\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(to_str(factorial(5)) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">120</pre></div></div><div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>struct.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">struct Point { x: int, y: int }\nfn manhattan(p: Point) -&gt; int {\n    return p.x + p.y;\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    let p: Point = Point { x: 3, y: 4 };\n    print(to_str(manhattan(p)) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">7</pre></div></div><div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>enum_and_match.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">enum Shape { Circle(int), Square(int), Empty }\nfn area(s: Shape) -&gt; int {\n    let mut a: int = 0;\n    match s {\n        Shape.Circle(r) =&gt; { a = 3 * r * r; }\n        Shape.Square(w) =&gt; { a = w * w; }\n        Shape.Empty =&gt; { a = 0; }\n    }\n    return a;\n}\nfn main() -&gt; int {\n    print(to_str(area(Shape.Circle(5))) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    print(to_str(area(Shape.Square(4))) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    print(to_str(area(Shape.Empty)) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">75\n16\n0</pre></div></div><div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>loop.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">fn main() -&gt; int {\n    let mut i: int = 0;\n    let mut total: int = 0;\n    while i &lt; 5 {\n        total = total + i;\n        i = i + 1;\n    }\n    print(to_str(total) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">10</pre></div></div><div class=\"playground-grid\" style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\"><div class=\"pg-editor\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>list.rux</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">fn main() -&gt; int {\n    let xs: list[int] = list_new();\n    for i in 0..5 {\n        push(xs, i * i);\n    }\n    let mut sum: int = 0;\n    for v in xs {\n        sum = sum + v;\n    }\n    print(&quot;squares sum: &quot; + to_str(sum) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    print(&quot;length: &quot; + to_str(list_len(xs)) + &quot;\\n&quot;);\n    return 0;\n}\nreturn main();</pre></div><div class=\"pg-output\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><span>Output (verified)</span></div><pre class=\"pg-code\">squares sum: 30\nlength: 5</pre></div></div> </div> </section> </main>";
}
fn page_privacy() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container narrow\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Legal</p> <h1>Privacy policy</h1> <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted)\">Last updated: 2026-11-03</p> <p class=\"lead\">This website is designed to collect as little as possible.</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">What this site collects</h2> <p>\nrudralang.tech is a static website. It has no accounts, no login, no\n        contact forms, and no analytics or advertising trackers embedded by the\n        site. The site does not set tracking cookies.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">Hosting</h2> <p>\nThe site is served by a hosting provider that may process standard\n        technical request data (such as IP address and user agent) in server\n        logs for security and operation, under the provider's own policies.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">Downloads</h2> <p>\nInstaller downloads are served from GitHub Releases. Accessing those\n        files is subject to GitHub's privacy practices.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">Email</h2> <p>\nIf you email <a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>, we\n        use your message only to respond to your inquiry.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">Contact</h2> <p>Questions about this policy: <a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>.</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <p>This policy describes current site behavior and is not legal advice or a certification of compliance with any specific regulation.</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_rakshanex() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Parent organization</p> <img src=\"/rakshanex-logo.png\" alt=\"RAKSHANEX Technologies logo\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" style=\"border-radius:18px;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:1rem\"> <h1>RAKSHANEX Technologies</h1> <p class=\"lead\" style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\">\nRAKSHANEX Technologies is the organization behind RUDRA. RUDRA is a\n        RAKSHANEX Technologies product.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Attribution</h2> <p>Powered by RAKSHANEX Technologies.</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Product</h2> <p>\nRUDRA, the compiled systems language and its toolchain, is developed and\n        maintained under RAKSHANEX Technologies. Source distribution and\n        releases are available on the\n<a href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub repository</a>.\n</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\"> <h4>Contact</h4> <p>\nFor support and inquiries, email\n<a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>.\n          Additional official organization links will be listed here once\n          verified.\n</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_roadmap() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Roadmap</p> <h1>Development status and roadmap</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nEvery item carries an accurate status. This roadmap is descriptive of\n        the current verified state, not a promise of dates.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Verified and stable</h2> <div class=\"grid grid-2\"> <div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3>Compile and run a program</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">The released 1.1.0 compiler, ruxc, builds a .rux source file into a native Linux x86-64 executable. Run it with ./output.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> A sample suite compiled with the released ruxc and ran with the expected output; see the Transparency page.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> Linux x86-64 only. Imports resolve only for modules next to the source; the rudra wrapper copies the standard library there for you.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3>Self-hosting compiler</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">The RUDRA compiler is written in RUDRA and rebuilds itself into a byte-identical binary.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> The project team reproduced the byte-identical fixed point and ran the language and negative test suites (83 of 84 language tests exit 0, the remaining test returns a computed value by design; all 19 negative tests are rejected in the repository suite).</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> This is the project team&#39;s own verification, not an independent audit. Generics are erased; closures, traits and tuples are not implemented.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3>Static zero-dependency binaries</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">ruxc is a statically linked ELF written in RUDRA with no runtime dependencies, and it emits static ELF executables directly.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> <h3>Runtime safety checks</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Integer division by zero traps, list access is bounds-checked and lists are capped at 512 elements.</p> </div> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.2rem\">Partially verified (standard-library modules shipped in 1.1.0)</h2> <div class=\"grid grid-2\"> <div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>Channels (std/chan)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">A FIFO channel library carrying full 64-bit signed values, with blocking, non-blocking and timeout receive and explicit status codes.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> Values sent in order were received in order, and an empty channel reports a distinct status code on a non-blocking receive. Earlier measurements: boundary values including the 64-bit minimum and maximum round-trip exactly, and 5000 messages from a separate process arrived in order.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> Capacity is finite (about 64 KB by default, configurable). Channels are an ordinary module, not a language builtin.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>JSON (std/json)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">json_get reads a value from a JSON object by key and json_valid validates a document following RFC 8259.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> json_get returned the expected values for a string and an integer key, and json_valid accepted a good document and rejected a malformed one. A 51-case RFC 8259 conformance matrix passed 51 of 51 in the project&#39;s tests.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> No nesting-depth limit yet. Surrogate pairs are not fully decoded and raw UTF-8 bytes are not validated. There is no json_parse function.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>DNS resolution (std/dns)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Hostname resolution reads the system resolver configuration, uses timeouts, checks response IDs, follows CNAME chains and reports explicit error codes.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> dns_resolve returned 127.0.0.1 for localhost. 21 adversarial scenarios against a local test DNS server passed in the project&#39;s tests, including spoofed IDs, truncated, malformed and looping responses.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> IPv4 A records only. AAAA (IPv6) and TCP fallback are not supported and are reported as unsupported.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>HTTP helpers and sockets (std/http, std/net)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Request and response builders and parsers plus raw TCP socket calls, for plain HTTP to a numeric IP address.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> The request and response helpers produced and parsed the expected method, path, status and body.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> No http_get builtin and no HTTPS.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>P-384 ECDSA signatures (std/ecdsa384)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">ECDSA signature verification on the P-384 curve with strict input checks.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> Signatures generated by OpenSSL with three independent keys verified correctly, and 21 tampered or out-of-range signatures were rejected in the project&#39;s tests.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> About 2 seconds per verification on current hardware. Performance work is pending.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> <h3>X.509 certificate validation (std/x509*, std/certval)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">A strict, fail-closed certificate validator checks DER encoding, signatures, validity dates, hostnames, CA constraints, key usage, chain building and explicitly configured trust anchors.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> A real public certificate chain was authenticated against a root from the system trust store, on two machines, and more than 30 invalid cases were rejected in the project&#39;s tests.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> ECDSA P-256 and P-384 only. RSA, Ed25519 and P-521 certificates are rejected. No revocation checking. Not connected to TLS.</p> </div> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.2rem\">Planned and not yet verified</h2> <div class=\"grid grid-2\"> <div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-planned\">PLANNED</span> <h3>Authenticated HTTPS (TLS 1.3)</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">An encrypted TLS 1.3 handshake works in the standard library, but the server&#39;s identity is not verified during the connection.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> A live TLS 1.3 handshake reached encrypted application data. Certificate authentication exists separately but is not wired into the connection.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> Not secure HTTPS. The connection is encrypted but unauthenticated and must not be relied on against an active attacker.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-planned\">PLANNED</span> <h3>Mutex and shared-memory threads</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">There is no mutex module and no spawn builtin in the self-hosted compiler. Process-based concurrency exists in std/thread.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-off\">NOT VERIFIED</span> <h3>Missing language features</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">Traits, closures, tuples, fixed-size arrays, hex and binary literals and specialized generics are not implemented in the self-hosted compiler.</p> </div> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.6rem\">In the source repository, not yet released</h2> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:0.8rem\"> <p>These tools are written in RUDRA and exist in the source repository. None of them is part of the published 1.1.0 archive, which contains only ruxc, the rudra wrapper, the standard library and examples. They are expected to ship in a later release.</p> </div> <div class=\"grid grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"> <div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">SOURCE REPOSITORY, NOT RELEASED</span> <h3>Driver</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">A driver written in RUDRA with the commands rudra build, run, check, vscode-init, toolchain and version.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> Not in 1.1.0: the released rudra command only accepts a source file and an output name.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">SOURCE REPOSITORY, NOT RELEASED</span> <h3>Language server</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">lsp/serve.rux is a language server written in RUDRA that works with editors that have a built-in LSP client.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> It answers the standard initialize request with its capabilities.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> No released binary yet.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">SOURCE REPOSITORY, NOT RELEASED</span> <h3>Formatter and package tool</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">fmt/fmt.rux re-indents code and package-manager/ruxpkg.rux verifies a package manifest&#39;s module SHA-256.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Evidence:</strong> The formatter produces compilable output.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> The formatter only re-indents. The profiler and the package-registry server do not currently build.</p> </div><div class=\"card\"> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">SOURCE REPOSITORY, NOT RELEASED</span> <h3>VS Code extension and Ruxel Studio</h3> <p style=\"font-size:0.9rem\">A VS Code extension with grammar, snippets and a problem matcher (no JavaScript), and Ruxel Studio, a full-screen terminal IDE.</p> <p style=\"font-size:0.85rem\"><strong>Limits:</strong> Ruxel Studio is a terminal IDE; a graphical IDE does not exist yet.</p> </div> </div> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <h4>How items advance</h4> <p>An item moves to VERIFIED only after it is compiled, run and confirmed against a published release. See <a href=\"/transparency\">Transparency</a> for the evidence behind each status.</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_security() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container narrow\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Trust</p> <h1>Security policy</h1> <p class=\"lead\">We take security seriously and welcome responsible disclosure.</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Reporting a vulnerability</h2> <p>\nIf you believe you have found a security issue in the RUDRA toolchain or\n        this website, report it privately to\n<a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>. Please do not open\n        a public issue for suspected vulnerabilities before they are addressed.\n</p> <p>Include a clear description, the affected version (1.1.0 is the current release) and the file name of the archive you installed, and steps to reproduce.</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Scope</h2> <ul> <li>The distributed RUDRA toolchain (the ruxc compiler, the rudra wrapper and the bundled standard library).</li> <li>This website and its published assets.</li> </ul> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">What we do not claim</h2> <p>\nRUDRA is designed with memory safety in mind, but no software is\n        guaranteed free of defects or vulnerabilities. This page does not assert\n        any formal certification, audit, or warranty. Verified capabilities and\n        their limits are documented on the <a href=\"/transparency\">Transparency</a> page.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Checksums</h2> <p>\nEvery published installer has a SHA-256 checksum on the\n<a href=\"/downloads/\">Downloads</a> page. Verify your download before\n        installing.\n</p> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_terms() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container narrow\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Legal</p> <h1>Terms of use</h1> <p style=\"color:var(--text-muted)\">Last updated: 2026-11-03</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Website</h2> <p>\nThis website provides information and downloads for the RUDRA toolchain.\n        Content is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. Links to\n        external sites (such as GitHub) are governed by those sites' own terms.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">The RUDRA toolchain</h2> <p>\nUse of the RUDRA toolchain is governed by the RUDRA License, published in\n        the <a href=\"https://github.com/rakshanex/rudra\" rel=\"noopener\">repository</a>. In summary, the\n        binaries are free to download and use, including for commercial software,\n        while the compiler source is proprietary and the binaries may not be\n        reverse-engineered or resold. The programs you build are yours. The\n        license file is the authoritative text.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">No warranty</h2> <p>\nThe software and this website are provided without warranty. To the\n        extent permitted by law, the authors are not liable for any claim,\n        damages, or other liability arising from their use.\n</p> <h2 style=\"margin-top:1.6rem\">Contact</h2> <p>Questions: <a href=\"mailto:support@rudralang.tech\">support@rudralang.tech</a>.</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:2rem\"> <p>These terms are a plain-language summary for the website and are not a substitute for the authoritative LICENSE text, nor do they represent reviewed legal advice.</p> </div> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
fn page_transparency() -> str {
    return "<main id=\"main\">  <section class=\"section\"> <div class=\"container\"> <p class=\"eyebrow\">Transparency</p> <h1>Verification matrix and evidence</h1> <p class=\"lead\">\nThe statuses below come from testing of the released toolchain by the\n        project team. No capability is listed as working unless it was compiled\n        and run. This is not an independent third-party audit. Benchmarks are published on the <a href=\"/benchmarks/\">Benchmarks</a> page with their method and caveats. No download counts or community statistics are published.\n</p> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:1.5rem\"> <h4>What was tested</h4> <p>\nArchive <code>rudra-1.1.0-selfhost-linux-x86_64.tar.gz</code> (RUDRA 1.1.0, 242,197 bytes),\n          SHA256 <code style=\"word-break:break-all\">13c31b6cadb74404812783e369fde08032dd671085c384c279e900073a7043b2</code>,\n          checked on 2026-11-06. The Debian package <code>rudra-1.1.0-selfhost-amd64.deb</code> (170,308 bytes) has SHA256\n<code style=\"word-break:break-all\">902a3ea0e95fa7bd85e7a153d235de648a09981f5d85d4f5fc3accb7147f88f6</code>. Tests ran on Linux x86_64 with the ruxc binary from this release.\n</p> </div> <div class=\"callout callout-info\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"> <h4>Earlier releases</h4> <p>\nVersions 1.0.0 and 1.0.1 were an earlier, Rust-based toolchain (with macOS and Windows installers). They are not the current toolchain. The 1.1.0 self-hosted toolchain is Linux x86-64 only, and features of the earlier toolchain such as spawn, mutex, channel and http_get builtins do not exist in it. Tools in the source repository that are not yet released are listed on the\n<a href=\"/roadmap\">roadmap</a>.\n</p> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.2rem\">Feature matrix</h2> <table> <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th><th>API</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>Compile and run a program</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>ruxc &lt;file.rux&gt; &lt;output&gt;</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Convenience wrapper</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>rudra &lt;file.rux&gt; &lt;output&gt;</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Structs, enums and match</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>Shape.Circle(5)</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Division-by-zero trap and bounds-checked lists</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span></td> <td><span style=\"color:var(--text-faint)\">n/a</span></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Channels</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>import &quot;chan&quot;; chan_new(); chan_send_status(c, v); chan_recv_status(c, out)</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>JSON</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>import &quot;json&quot;; json_get(doc, key); json_valid(doc)</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>HTTP helpers (numeric IP)</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>import &quot;http&quot;; http_get_request(host, path)</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Hostname resolution (DNS)</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span></td> <td><code>import &quot;dns&quot;; dns_resolve(host)</code></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Threads and mutex builtins</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-off\">NOT VERIFIED</span></td> <td><span style=\"color:var(--text-faint)\">n/a</span></td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Authenticated HTTPS / TLS</strong></td> <td><span class=\"badge badge-planned\">PLANNED</span></td> <td><span style=\"color:var(--text-faint)\">n/a</span></td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.2rem\">Evidence</h2> <div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Compile and run a program</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">Programs compiled with the released ruxc and ran with the expected output. For example, a hello program printed Hello, RUDRA! with exit code 0, and the rudra wrapper (rudra hello.rux hello, then ./hello) produced the same result.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Structs, enums and match</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">A program computing areas from a payload enum (Shape.Circle(5), Shape.Square(4), Shape.Empty) printed 75, 16 and 0, and a struct sample printed 7.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Division-by-zero trap and bounds-checked lists</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-verified\">VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">A program that divides by a runtime zero terminated abnormally (exit status 134) instead of continuing, and reading list index 5 of a one-element list also terminated abnormally.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Channels</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">Three values sent with chan_send_status were received in the same order (100, 200, 300), and a further non-blocking receive on the empty channel returned status 2. Capacity is finite; behaviour under heavy load was not exercised in this verification.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">JSON</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">json_get on a JSON object returned the expected string and integer values, json_valid accepted a well-formed document and rejected a malformed one. Arrays and nested lookups were not exercised.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">HTTP helpers (numeric IP)</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">http_get_request built a GET request that http_req_method and http_req_path parsed back, and http_response with http_resp_status and http_resp_body round-tripped a 200 response. A live request against a server was not exercised in this verification.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Hostname resolution (DNS)</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-partial\">PARTIALLY VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">dns_resolve(&quot;localhost&quot;) returned 127.0.0.1 and dns_aaaa_supported() returned false. Resolution against public DNS servers was not exercised in this verification.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Threads and mutex builtins</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-off\">NOT VERIFIED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">The self-hosted compiler has no spawn, mutex_new, lock or unlock builtin. Only fork-based process helpers exist in std/thread.</p> </div><div class=\"card\" style=\"margin-top:0.9rem\"> <div style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap\"> <h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:1.05rem\">Authenticated HTTPS / TLS</h3> <span class=\"badge badge-planned\">PLANNED</span> </div> <p style=\"font-size:0.92rem;margin:0.6rem 0 0\">TLS 1.3 and X.509 modules ship in the standard library, but certificate authentication is not wired into a live client. No authenticated HTTPS is claimed.</p> </div> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2.5rem\">Known discrepancies and limitations</h2> <ul> <li>The released ruxc is a <strong>statically linked</strong> x86-64 ELF with no runtime dependencies. Earlier site text that described dynamically linked binaries applied to the previous Rust-based toolchain and has been corrected.</li> <li>The only released command forms are <code>ruxc &lt;file.rux&gt; &lt;output&gt;</code> and <code>rudra &lt;file.rux&gt; &lt;output&gt;</code>. There is no <code>--run</code> or <code>-o</code> flag, and no <code>rudra new</code>, <code>build</code>, <code>check</code>, <code>clean</code>, <code>doctor</code>, <code>run</code> or <code>version</code> command in 1.1.0.</li> <li>A program runs its top-level statements. A file that only defines <code>fn main()</code> compiles but prints nothing; end the file with <code>return main();</code>.</li> <li>print takes only a str; convert integers with <code>to_str(n)</code>, and add <code>\"\\n\"</code> yourself.</li> <li>Imports resolve only for modules in the same directory as the source. The rudra wrapper copies the standard library there.</li> <li>Traits, impl blocks, closures, tuples, fixed-size arrays, hex and binary literals, block comments and const are not implemented. Generics syntax is accepted but erased.</li> <li>Option and Result are not built-in types, and the <code>?</code> operator is not a built-in feature.</li> <li>Channels, JSON, HTTP helpers and DNS are standard-library modules with their own function names; there are no http_get, json_get, spawn or mutex builtins.</li> <li>No guarantee is made that the software is free of defects or vulnerabilities.</li> </ul> <h2 style=\"margin-top:2rem\">Status definitions</h2> <ul> <li><strong>VERIFIED</strong> - compiled and run with the expected result.</li> <li><strong>PARTIALLY VERIFIED</strong> - present and runs, but a part of the claim was not fully exercised.</li> <li><strong>PLANNED</strong> - documented as roadmap, not shipped.</li> <li><strong>NOT VERIFIED</strong> - could not be confirmed, or observed not to work as documented.</li> </ul> </div> </section>  </main>";
}
